 "why": "The FEM gets a time simulation in 2.9.0 (step responses, animation, power profiles): the time to 63 % of its step response (hottest column cell of the footprint, Crank-Nicolson with the Rannacher start, the response cell 2 mm) is ADDED for the boards whose FEM mesh at that cell is at most the harness cap FEM_TIME_CAP (50 000 unknowns; every one takes the direct path, the reference board above the steady direct limit); no existing record moves. Regenerated on the tree of fix/fem-thin-copper-source: the part now enters the FEM through its outer face on every outer copper layer, which moves these times by 1e-6 to 2e-5 of their value (3e-3 on drawn_ell) (the steady records that move are in fem-thin-copper-source.json); one record, one file."
